   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to repeal sections 2, 3, 4, and 5 of chapter 330 of the laws of 2011\namending the town law relating to payments for certain school, fire, fire\nprotection, and ambulance districts for lands exempt from real property\ntaxation for purposes which implement the Peconic Bay community preservation\nfund; and providing for the repeal of certain provisions upon expiration\nthereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S8025",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8025-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Rpld §§2, 3, 4 & 5, Chap 330 of 2011",
    "lawSection": "Towns",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8025\n\nSPONSOR: PALUMBO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to repeal sections 2, 3, 4, and 5 of chapter 330 of the laws of\n2011 amending the town law relating to payments for certain school,\nfire, fire protection, and ambulance districts for lands exempt from\nreal property taxation for purposes which implement the Peconic Bay\ncommunity preservation fund; and providing for the repeal of certain\nprovisions upon expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nPermits a town to make annual payments from its Community Preservation\nFund (CP) enacted pursuant to section 64-e of the town law to school,\ndire, fire protection and ambulance districts to mitigate the impact of\nlost tax revenues from lands made wholly exempt as a result of their\nacquisition by the federal, state, or local government for the preserva-\ntion of community character.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Repeals sections 2, 3,4 and 5 of Chapter 330 of the Laws of\n2011 amending the town law relating to payments for certain school,\nfire, fire protection and ambulance districts for lands exempt from real\nproperty taxation for purposes which implement the Peconic Bay Community\nPreservation Fund.\n\nSection 2. Permits a town to make annual payments from its CPF enacted\npursuant to section 64-e of the town law to school, fire, fire\nprotection and ambulance districts.\n\nSection 3. Provides that CPF payments made by a town pursuant to this\nsection shall only be made for lands within school, fire, fire\nprotection and ambulance districts which are wholly exempt from real\nproperty taxation pursuant to the real property law that have been\nacquired by the federal government, state government or a municipal\ncorporation for community preservation purposes pursuant to section 64e\nof the town law regardless of whether said lands were acquired with CPF\nmonies. It also establishes criteria for determining the payment for\neach eligible district.\n\nSection 4. Relates to instances where the total annual budget appropri-\nation by a town for payments under this act is less than the aggregate\npayments for all districts.\n\nSection 5. Requires the adoption of an annual plan by the town board\nbefore payments authorized by the act can be made.\n\nSection 6. Effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe towns of East Hampton, Southampton, Riverhead, Shelter Island and\nSouthold have established CPFs pursuant to section 64-e of the town law\n(Peconic Bay Community Preservation Fund). This legislation would give\nthese towns the ability to provide relief to eligible school, fire, fire\nprotection and ambulance district that incurred extraordinary financial\nhardship as a result of lost revenues caused by removing such lands from\nthe tax rolls for CPF purposes, by permitting them to receive payments\nfrom the CPF\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately, provided, however, that sections\n2, 3, 4 and 5 of this act shall expire and be deemed repealed December\n31, 2050.\n",
